task:
`sqlparse.split` mishandles `BEGIN TRANSACTION` / `END TRANSACTION`, treating BEGIN as the start of a block so the statements aren't split.
Repro: `sqlparse.split('BEGIN TRANSACTION;
DELETE FROM "schema"."table_a" USING "table_a_temp" WHERE ...;
INSERT INTO "schema"."table_a" SELECT * FROM "table_a_temp";
END TRANSACTION;')`.
Expected 4 statements: 'BEGIN TRANSACTION;', the DELETE, the INSERT, 'END TRANSACTION;'. The same applies when a newline separates the words (`BEGIN
TRANSACTION;` ... `END
TRANSACTION;`), with statements 'BEGIN
TRANSACTION;' and 'END
TRANSACTION;'.
